[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523102918","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100094#issuecomment-2523102918","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100094","id":2523102918,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WY37G","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T12:22:14Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T12:22:14Z","body":"This is because the `_ready` method (where you're setting the `world_2d` property) gets called *after* the child nodes are ready (by that time, they will have been added to the other physics space). As a workaround, you can save the nodes under `SubViewport` into their own scene, remove the instance of that scene in the editor, and instead instantiate that scene dynamically and add it as a child *after* setting the `world_2d`:\n\n```gdscript\n\tskin_sub_viewport_container_sub_viewport.world_2d = World2D.new()\n\n\tskin_sub_viewport_container_sub_viewport.add_child(load(\"res://node_2d.tscn\").instantiate())\n\n\tvar skin_sub_viewport_container_animatable_body = $SkinSubViewportContainer/SubViewport/Node2D/AnimatableBody2D\n\tvar skin_canvas_group_animatable_body = $SkinCanvasGroup/Node2D/AnimatableBody2D\n\n        ...\n```\n\nIt's strange that `world_2d` can't be set in the inspector, seems inconsistent with 3D.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523102918/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523115702","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100094#issuecomment-2523115702","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100094","id":2523115702,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6WY7C2","user":{"login":"razcore-rad","id":1177508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzc1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1177508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/razcore-rad","html_url":"https://github.com/razcore-rad","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razcore-rad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razcore-rad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razcore-rad/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razcore-rad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razcore-rad/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razcore-rad/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razcore-rad/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razcore-rad/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/razcore-rad/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-06T12:29:50Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T12:29:50Z","body":"Indeed, thanks, I can confirm that this fixes it. Also yes, `world_2d` can't be set from Inspector so it is an inconsistency :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2523115702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]